# name: test/sql/markdown_table_extraction_fallible.test
# description: The table extractors' inline depth cap stays an Invalid Input Error on DuckDB v2.0
# group: [sql]

require markdown

# =============================================================================
# md_extract_table_rows and md_extract_tables_json reach an InvalidInputException
# two calls down: the callback calls ExtractTables, ExtractTables calls
# GetInlineText on every cell, and GetInlineText throws past MAX_INLINE_DEPTH
# (src/markdown_utils.cpp). Neither function declared SetFallible().
#
# On v1.5 that makes no difference to the error. On v2.0 it does. DuckDB
# v2.0-cyanoptera, src/function/scalar_function.cpp:
#
#   void ThrowNonFallibleFunctionError(const Identifier &name, std::exception &ex) {
#       ErrorData error(ex);
#       if (!Exception::IsExecutionError(error.Type())) {
#           throw;
#       }
#       throw InternalException("Scalar function \"%s\" threw an execution error, but the "
#                               "function is not marked as fallible - ...");
#
# and src/common/exception.cpp limits IsExecutionError to INVALID_INPUT,
# OUT_OF_RANGE and CONVERSION. The depth cap exists to turn unbounded recursion
# into a readable message, and an unmarked function turns that message into an
# INTERNAL error instead.
#
# THE EXPECTATION PINS THE ERROR CLASS, NOT JUST THE TEXT. The INTERNAL form
# quotes the original message after "Error: ", so a bare substring match on
# "Markdown inline nesting exceeds" passes on both lines and discriminates
# nothing. Only the "Invalid Input Error: " prefix fails on an unmarked v2.0
# build. That is also why the case below is an InvalidInputException: an
# IOException passes through ThrowNonFallibleFunctionError unchanged, so it
# cannot tell the two apart (duck_block_utils, measured on v2.0-cyanoptera,
# 2026-09-14).
#
# THE INPUT IS NESTED IMAGES. Each `![` opens an image node that GetInlineText
# recurses into, so 1001 of them reach depth 1001. Alternating emphasis
# (`*_*_...`) and nested strikethrough do not reach the cap at 1001 or 3000;
# cmark does not build them that deep. That was measured on the v1.5.5 build.
# This file passes on v1.5 with or without the fix. Only the v2.0 build can
# fail it.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Boundary: depth 1000 is within the cap, and both functions return the table.

query I
SELECT len(md_extract_table_rows(('| h |' || chr(10) || '|---|' || chr(10) || '| ' || repeat('![', 1000) || 'x' || repeat('](u)', 1000) || ' |')::MARKDOWN));
----
2

query I
SELECT len(md_extract_tables_json(('| h |' || chr(10) || '|---|' || chr(10) || '| ' || repeat('![', 1000) || 'x' || repeat('](u)', 1000) || ' |')::MARKDOWN));
----
1

# ---- Depth 1001: the cap fires, and it must surface as Invalid Input on every line.

statement error
SELECT md_extract_table_rows(('| h |' || chr(10) || '|---|' || chr(10) || '| ' || repeat('![', 1001) || 'x' || repeat('](u)', 1001) || ' |')::MARKDOWN);
----
Invalid Input Error: Markdown inline nesting exceeds maximum supported depth (1000)

statement error
SELECT md_extract_tables_json(('| h |' || chr(10) || '|---|' || chr(10) || '| ' || repeat('![', 1001) || 'x' || repeat('](u)', 1001) || ' |')::MARKDOWN);
----
Invalid Input Error: Markdown inline nesting exceeds maximum supported depth (1000)
